  ApiClient.get never throws — it always returns Either<Failure, T>.

  lib/core/network/api_client.dart:43-52 — `get()` delegates to the private `_send` helper (no try/catch of its own, none needed since `_send` owns it).

  lib/core/network/api_client.dart:276-293 — `_send`'s full try/catch:
  ```
  try {
    final response = await request();
    final data = response.data;
    if (data == null) {
      return left(const Failure.malformedResponse(message: 'Empty response body'));
    }
    return right(data);
  } on DioException catch (e) {
    return left(_mapDioException(e));
  } catch (e) {
    return left(Failure.malformedResponse(message: e.toString()));
  }
  ```
  The generic `catch (e)` (not just `on DioException`) guarantees every exception, Dio or otherwise, is mapped to `Left<Failure>`. A doc comment at api_client.dart:21 states this explicitly: "no dio/native exception ever escapes unmapped (RNF09)."

  Checked 3 callers — none wrap `_apiClient.get` itself in try/catch; their try/catches are only around local JSON decoding of the already-unwrapped success value:
  - lib/features/entries/data/datasources/entries_remote_data_source.dart:75-96 (`list`) — `await _apiClient.get(...)` bare at line 75, `try` only starts at 86 inside `result.flatMap`.
  - lib/features/entries/data/datasources/entries_remote_data_source.dart:108-113 (`get`) — same pattern.
  - lib/features/export/data/datasources/export_remote_data_source.dart:66-74 (`getStatus`) — same pattern.
  - lib/features/dashboard/data/datasources/dashboard_remote_data_source.dart:20-29 (`getAggregate`) — same pattern.

  Confirms codebase-wide convention: `ApiClient.get` never throws.

